{"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04T0", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{proposition-algebraic-stack-no-automorphisms}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5f763c3f6164cbee6468562c40014d26b5865cb9b76089b2e57110e538bdce5b", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis lemma is a generalization of\nProposition <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:443ae7e83cb9d69c3392e61cdce99bcacf6d0ad0e6889a58608ac4a904277cc9", "unit_id": "tag:04T0:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04T0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sch_{fppf}$", "MATH_0003": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0004": "$1$", "MATH_0005": "$S$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\in \\Ob((\\Sch/S)_{fppf})$", "MATH_0007": "$f : \\mathcal{X}_U \\to \\mathcal{Y}_U$", "MATH_0008": "$f$", "MATH_0009": "$f$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-characterize-representable-by-algebraic-spaces}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:50d2342efbe7479a70fdc962a7b1d87c56cdad3c171c964bb9e3a6a8efde9003", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5711c148185a6d14e0c35aa93abfba5da55e15fe3b9d179cd12b6fa74b2ed894", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme contained in <MATH_0002>.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a <MATH_0004>-morphism of algebraic\nstacks over <MATH_0005>. The following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> for <MATH_0006>\nthe functor <MATH_0007> is faithful,\n<STRUCT_0003> the functor <MATH_0008> is faithful, and\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0009> is representable by algebraic spaces.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b9d4bc18426355ac095e982ed8afb78b34fb301a1eb1e566efa7de0fef27a1ce", "unit_id": "tag:04Y5:statement"}
{"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04T0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$1$", "MATH_0002": "$U$", "MATH_0003": "$y \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{Y}_U)$", "MATH_0004": "$$\n\\mathcal{W} = (\\Sch/U)_{fppf} \\times_{y, \\mathcal{Y}} \\mathcal{X}\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$U$", "MATH_0006": "$(\\Sch/U)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{W}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{W}$", "MATH_0009": "$(V, x, \\alpha : y(V) \\to f(x))$", "MATH_0010": "$f$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{W}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{W}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-lemma-equivalence-fibred-categories}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-criterion-map-representable-spaces-fibred-in-groupoids}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-2-fibre-product}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{proposition-algebraic-stack-no-automorphisms}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:274ba355c36a3e05f856e2bd04f6b1ef3727f463e764360c074699f65c6fef75", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:af8235a505b357b386d688a02a4d5808a1ab93cf53205189300d0b66493ec0a8", "source_text": "Parts (1) and (2) are equivalent by general properties of <MATH_0001>-morphisms\nof categories fibred in groupoids, see\nCategories, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nWe see that (3) implies (2) by\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nFinally, assume (2).\nLet <MATH_0002> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0003>.\nWe have to prove that\n<MATH_0004>\nis representable by an algebraic space over <MATH_0005>. Since\n<MATH_0006> is an algebraic stack we see from\nLemma <REF_0003>\nthat <MATH_0007> is an algebraic stack.\nOn the other hand the explicit description of objects of <MATH_0008>\nas triples <MATH_0009> and the fact that <MATH_0010> is\nfaithful, shows that the fibre categories of <MATH_0011> are setoids. Hence\nProposition <REF_0004>\nguarantees that <MATH_0012> is representable by an algebraic space.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:676b163b31ccdcf92eecfd69d2ae10496f339f8c544ede8546e9de7a87e32969", "unit_id": "tag:04Y5:proof"}
